\ Deadline: the pictures of the ground floor's rooms, besides the Foyer: the
\ halls north and south of the stairs, the stairs and their landing, the
\ living room, the corner, the dining room, the kitchen and pantry, and Mrs.
\ Rourke's rooms and the south closet. Furniture is placed as people are, by
\ a spot and a heading, in its own measure of metres right, up and forward.

\ === pieces of furniture and rooms ===

\ a box in a thing's own measure, between two corners [ right up forward ], placed at a spot facing a heading; filled black so it hides what is behind it
: turned-box ( near far spot heading -- )
	| near far spot heading |
	near spread to f0 to u0 to r0
	far spread to f1 to u1 to r1
	[ [ r0 u0 f0 ] [ r1 u0 f0 ] [ r1 u0 f1 ] [ r0 u0 f1 ]
	  [ r0 u1 f0 ] [ r1 u1 f0 ] [ r1 u1 f1 ] [ r0 u1 f1 ] ]
	( corner | corner spot heading placed ) map to c
	[ [ 0 1 2 3 ] [ 4 5 6 7 ] [ 0 1 5 4 ] [ 1 2 6 5 ] [ 2 3 7 6 ] [ 3 0 4 7 ] ]
	( face | face ( c swap @i ) map 0 fill ) each
	[ c 0 @i c 1 @i c 2 @i c 3 @i ] outline
	[ c 4 @i c 5 @i c 6 @i c 7 @i ] outline
	0 4 1 do k c k @i c k 4 + @i segment loop ;

\ lines through points in a thing's own measure
: turned-path ( points spot heading -- )
	| points spot heading |
	points ( point | point spot heading placed ) map path ;

\ a point on a wall: from an origin, along the wall by a and up by b
: wall-at ( origin along a b -- point )
	| origin along a b |
	[ 0 3 1 do k origin k @i along k @i a * + k 1 = if b + then loop ] ;

\ an opening in a wall from one floor point to another, dark within, its frame drawn
: open-doorway ( x0 z0 x1 z1 height -- )
	| x0 z0 x1 z1 height |
	[ [ x0 0 z0 ] [ x1 0 z1 ] [ x1 height z1 ] [ x0 height z0 ] ] 0 fill
	[ [ x0 0 z0 ] [ x0 height z0 ] [ x1 height z1 ] [ x1 0 z1 ] ] path ;

\ a panelled door in a wall from its hinge [ x0 z0 ] to its latch side [ x1 z1 ]; open, it swings into the room on the side given by a unit direction [ into-x into-z ]
: wall-panel-door ( x0 z0 x1 z1 height open into-x into-z -- )
	| x0 z0 x1 z1 height open into-x into-z |
	x1 x0 - to along-x
	z1 z0 - to along-z
	along-x sq along-z sq + sqrt to width
	open if
		pen to frame-light
		x0 z0 x1 z1 height open-doorway
		x0 along-x 0.34 * + into-x width 0.94 * * + to leaf-x
		z0 along-z 0.34 * + into-z width 0.94 * * + to leaf-z
		[ [ x0 0.02 z0 ] [ leaf-x 0.02 leaf-z ] [ leaf-x height 0.04 - leaf-z ] [ x0 height 0.04 - z0 ] ] 0 fill
		frame-light 1.2 * pen!
		[ [ x0 0.02 z0 ] [ leaf-x 0.02 leaf-z ] [ leaf-x height 0.04 - leaf-z ] [ x0 height 0.04 - z0 ] ] outline
		frame-light pen!
		exit
	then
	[ [ x0 0 z0 ] [ x1 0 z1 ] [ x1 height z1 ] [ x0 height z0 ] ] 0 fill
	[ [ x0 0 z0 ] [ x1 0 z1 ] [ x1 height z1 ] [ x0 height z0 ] ] outline
	pen to frame-light
	frame-light 0.55 * pen!
	[ 0.12 0.55 ] ( bottom |
		[ x0 0 z0 ] to base
		[ along-x width / 0 along-z width / ] to along
		bottom 0.55 = if height 0.12 - else height 0.5 * then to top
		[ base along width 0.18 * bottom height * wall-at
		  base along width 0.82 * bottom height * wall-at
		  base along width 0.82 * top wall-at
		  base along width 0.18 * top wall-at ] outline
	) each
	frame-light 1.4 * pen!
	[ x0 0 z0 ] [ along-x width / 0 along-z width / ] width 0.88 * height 0.47 * wall-at to knob
	knob [ knob 0 @i along-x width / 0.03 * + knob 1 @i knob 2 @i along-z width / 0.03 * + ] segment
	frame-light pen! ;

\ floor boards running along one axis between a room's walls, spacing apart
: plank-floor ( west east south north spacing along-z -- )
	| west east south north spacing along-z |
	along-z if
		east west - spacing / round-down to n-boards
		0 n-boards 1 + 1 do k
			k spacing * west + to x
			x 0 south x 0 north edge
		loop
	else
		north south - spacing / round-down to n-boards
		0 n-boards 1 + 1 do k
			k spacing * south + to z
			west 0 z east 0 z edge
		loop
	then ;

\ a long rug with a border inset inside it, lying on the floor
: runner-rug ( west east south north -- )
	| west east south north |
	[ [ west 0.01 south ] [ east 0.01 south ] [ east 0.01 north ] [ west 0.01 north ] ] 0.03 fill
	[ [ west 0.01 south ] [ east 0.01 south ] [ east 0.01 north ] [ west 0.01 north ] ] outline
	pen to rug-light
	rug-light 0.6 * pen!
	[ [ west 0.1 + 0.012 south 0.1 + ] [ east 0.1 - 0.012 south 0.1 + ]
	  [ east 0.1 - 0.012 north 0.1 - ] [ west 0.1 + 0.012 north 0.1 - ] ] outline
	rug-light pen! ;

\ a lamp hanging on a cord from the ceiling, with its shade and its glow
: pendant-lamp ( x y z ceiling -- )
	| x y z ceiling |
	[ x y 0.1 - z ] 1.1 0.3 glow
	0.4 pen!
	x ceiling z x y z edge
	0.75 pen!
	x y z 0.05 8 ring to shade-top
	x y 0.18 - z 0.16 12 ring to shade-bottom
	shade-bottom outline
	0 12 3 do k shade-top k 2 / round-down @i shade-bottom k @i segment loop
	shade-top outline ;

\ a flight of stairs from a spot, rising along a heading: count steps of run and rise, a width wide to the right, solid black, the nosing of each step drawn bright and the risers and sides faint
: stair-flight ( spot heading width run rise count -- )
	| spot heading width run rise count |
	pen to nosing-light
	count rise * 0 min2 to bottom
	[ 0 1 ] ( side |
		side width * to across
		[ [ across bottom count run * ] [ across bottom 0 ] [ across 0 0 ]
		  0 count 1 do k [ across k 1 + rise * k run * ] [ across k 1 + rise * k 1 + run * ] loop
		] ( point | point spot heading placed ) map to profile
		profile 0 fill
		nosing-light 0.4 * pen!
		profile outline
	) each
	( point | point spot heading placed ) to placing
	count 1 - -1 -1 do k
		[ [ 0 k rise * k run * ] [ width k rise * k run * ] [ width k 1 + rise * k run * ] [ 0 k 1 + rise * k run * ] ]
		placing map 0 fill
		[ [ 0 k 1 + rise * k run * ] [ width k 1 + rise * k run * ] [ width k 1 + rise * k 1 + run * ] [ 0 k 1 + rise * k 1 + run * ] ]
		placing map 0 fill
		nosing-light 0.35 * pen!
		[ [ 0 k rise * k run * ] [ width k rise * k run * ] ] spot heading turned-path
		nosing-light pen!
		[ [ 0 k 1 + rise * k run * ] [ width k 1 + rise * k run * ] ] spot heading turned-path
	loop
	nosing-light pen! ;

\ a banister beside a flight of stairs, on the side at right, from the newel post up the flight
: banister ( spot heading right run rise count -- )
	| spot heading right run rise count |
	[ right 0.05 - 0 -0.05 ] [ right 0.05 + 1.05 0.05 ] spot heading turned-box
	[ [ right 0.95 0 ] [ right count rise * 0.9 + count run * ] ] spot heading turned-path
	pen to rail-light
	rail-light 0.55 * pen!
	0 count 1 do k
		k 1 + rise * to tread
		k 0.5 + run * to middle
		[ [ right tread middle ] [ right middle rise * run / 0.95 + middle ] ] spot heading turned-path
	loop
	rail-light pen! ;

\ the light a pane of a south window lets fall on the floor, falling north and a little west, with faint shafts from the pane down to it
: south-pane-light ( west east bottom top z -- )
	| west east bottom top z |
	[ [ west bottom z ] [ east bottom z ] [ east top z ] [ west top z ] ] to pane
	pane ( corner | corner spread to cz to y to x [ x y 0.3 * - 0 cz y 1.1 * + ] ) map to patch
	patch 0.08 fill
	0.16 pen!
	patch 0 @i patch 1 @i patch 2 @i patch 3 @i 5 hatch
	0.035 pen!
	0 4 1 do k pane k @i patch k @i segment loop ;

\ === North of Foyer ===

\ the hall north of the foyer, seen from its south end: the living room's doorway to the west, the foot of the stairs to the east, the hall going on north
: nfoyer-picture ( -- )
	0.15 1.65 -1.2 0 -0.05 240 new-picture
	[ 0 2.7 3.2 ] lamp!
	[ [ [ 0.35 0 3.9 ] PI 0.1 + ] [ [ -0.45 0 5.1 ] PI 0.15 - ] [ [ 0.55 0 2.6 ] PI 0.25 + ] ] spots!
	0.1 pen!
	-1.3 1.3 0 7 0.25 true plank-floor
	0.25 pen!
	-0.55 0.55 0.8 6.4 runner-rug
	[ 0 0 3.2 ] 1.3 0.08 glow
	0.12 pen!
	-1.3 0 7 -1.3 0 10 edge
	1.3 0 7 1.3 0 10 edge
	-1.3 3 7 -1.3 3 10 edge
	1.3 3 7 1.3 3 10 edge
	[ [ -1.3 0 10 ] [ 1.3 0 10 ] [ 1.3 3 10 ] [ -1.3 3 10 ] ] outline
	0.45 pen!
	[ [ -1.3 0 0 ] [ -1.3 0 7 ] ] path
	[ [ 1.3 0 0 ] [ 1.3 0 7 ] ] path
	[ [ -1.3 3.2 0 ] [ -1.3 3.2 7 ] [ 1.3 3.2 7 ] [ 1.3 3.2 0 ] ] path
	-1.3 3.2 7 -1.3 0 7 edge
	1.3 3.2 7 1.3 0 7 edge
	-1.3 3 7 1.3 3 7 edge
	0.2 pen!
	-1.3 0.95 0 -1.3 0.95 2.1 edge
	-1.3 0.95 3.5 -1.3 0.95 7 edge
	1.3 0.95 0 1.3 0.95 2.2 edge
	1.3 0.95 4.4 1.3 0.95 7 edge
	0.5 pen!
	-1.3 2.1 -1.3 3.5 2.4 open-doorway
	0.1 pen!
	-1.3 0 2.3 -2.6 0 2.1 edge
	-1.3 0 3.3 -2.6 0 3.5 edge
	[ -2.4 1.1 2.8 ] 0.9 0.06 glow
	0.5 pen!
	1.3 2.2 1.3 4.4 2.7 open-doorway
	0.45 pen!
	[ 1.35 0 4.3 ] PI 2 / 1.9 0.28 0.18 6 stair-flight
	0 2.72 3.2 3.2 pendant-lamp ;

\ === Bottom of Stairs ===

\ the foot of the staircase, seen from the archway to the west: the stairs climbing east, the archway to the south hall on the right
: stair-bottom-picture ( -- )
	-2.2 1.65 0 PI 2 / 0.08 - -0.02 290 new-picture
	[ 0.5 2.9 0.5 ] lamp!
	[ [ [ -0.2 0 0.4 ] PI 2 / PI + 0.1 - ] [ [ 0.3 0 -0.8 ] PI 2 / PI + 0.35 - ] [ [ -0.9 0 1.0 ] PI 2 / PI + 0.25 + ] ] spots!
	0.1 pen!
	-2.4 3 -1.6 1.6 0.25 false plank-floor
	[ 0.4 0 0.2 ] 1.6 0.08 glow
	0.45 pen!
	[ [ -2.4 0 1.6 ] [ 3 0 1.6 ] [ 3 3.4 1.6 ] [ -2.4 3.4 1.6 ] ] path
	[ [ -2.4 0 -1.6 ] [ 3 0 -1.6 ] [ 3 3.4 -1.6 ] [ -2.4 3.4 -1.6 ] ] path
	3 0 -1.6 3 0 1.6 edge
	3 3.4 -1.6 3 3.4 1.6 edge
	0.2 pen!
	-2.4 0.95 1.6 -0.4 0.95 1.6 edge
	-2.4 0.95 -1.6 0.2 0.95 -1.6 edge
	1.6 0.95 -1.6 3 0.95 -1.6 edge
	[ [ 0.2 0 -1.6 ]
	  0 12 1 do k k 11 / PI * to angle [ 0.9 angle cos 0.7 * - 2.1 angle sin 0.7 * + -1.6 ] loop
	  [ 1.6 0 -1.6 ] ] to arch
	arch 0 fill
	0.55 pen!
	arch path
	0.1 pen!
	0.3 0 -1.6 0.3 0 -3.6 edge
	1.5 0 -1.6 1.5 0 -3.6 edge
	[ 0.9 1.3 -3.3 ] 0.8 0.05 glow
	0.4 pen!
	2.3 0 0.25 3 1.62 1.5 solid-box
	[ [ 3 1.62 0.25 ] [ 3 1.62 1.5 ] [ 3 3.4 1.5 ] [ 3 3.4 0.25 ] ] 0 fill
	[ [ 3 1.62 0.25 ] [ 3 3.4 0.25 ] ] path
	0.55 pen!
	[ -0.4 0 1.5 ] PI 2 / 1.25 0.3 0.18 9 stair-flight
	0.6 pen!
	[ -0.4 0 1.5 ] PI 2 / 1.3 0.3 0.18 9 banister
	0.5 2.95 0.3 3.4 pendant-lamp ;

\ === the Stairs ===

\ the landing halfway up, seen looking back west: the lower flight falling away on the right, the upper flight climbing on the left, a rail between them, and the blinds of the window behind striping the landing and the stairwell's end wall with light
: stairs-picture ( -- )
	1.3 1.65 0.3 PI -2 / 0.05 + -0.3 250 new-picture
	[ 3 2 0 ] lamp!
	[ [ [ -0.9 0 -0.6 ] PI 2 / 0.15 - ] [ [ -0.7 0 0.9 ] PI 2 / 0.3 + ] ] spots!
	0.4 pen!
	-4 -1.6 -1.6 -4 3.2 -1.6 edge
	[ [ -4 -1.6 -1.6 ] [ -4 -1.6 1.6 ] [ -4 4.8 1.6 ] [ -4 4.8 -1.6 ] ] outline
	[ -4 0.4 -1.1 ] [ -4 2.9 -1.1 ] [ -4 2.7 1.1 ] [ -4 0.2 1.1 ] 7 0.09 blind-light
	0.4 pen!
	[ [ 1.6 0 -1.6 ] [ -4 0 -1.6 ] ] path
	[ [ 1.6 0 1.6 ] [ -1.6 0 1.6 ] [ -4 -1.6 1.6 ] ] path
	[ [ 1.6 3.2 -1.6 ] [ -1.6 3.2 -1.6 ] [ -4 4.8 -1.6 ] ] path
	[ [ 1.6 3.2 1.6 ] [ -1.6 3.2 1.6 ] [ -4 3.2 1.6 ] ] path
	[ [ 1.6 0 -1.6 ] [ 1.6 0 1.6 ] ] path
	[ 1.5 0.005 -0.7 ] [ -1.5 0.005 -1.0 ] [ -1.5 0.005 1.0 ] [ 1.5 0.005 0.7 ] 8 0.12 blind-light
	0.55 pen!
	[ -1.6 0 0.1 ] PI -2 / 1.4 0.28 -0.18 8 stair-flight
	[ -1.6 0 -1.5 ] PI -2 / 1.4 0.28 0.18 8 stair-flight
	0.6 pen!
	[ -1.6 0 -1.5 ] PI -2 / 1.45 0.28 0.18 8 banister
	[ -1.6 0 0.1 ] PI -2 / -0.05 0.28 -0.18 8 banister ;

\ === the south halls ===

\ a lamp on a wall facing a direction [ out-x out-z ], its bracket and shade, and the glow it casts
: hallway-sconce ( x y z out-x out-z -- )
	| x y z out-x out-z |
	[ x out-x 0.14 * + y 0.05 + z out-z 0.14 * + ] 0.8 0.28 glow
	0.4 pen!
	x y 0.1 - z x out-x 0.14 * + y 0.1 - z out-z 0.14 * + edge
	0.75 pen!
	x out-x 0.14 * + y 0.12 + z out-z 0.14 * + 0.07 8 ring outline
	x out-x 0.14 * + y 0.04 - z out-z 0.14 * + 0.04 8 ring outline ;

\ a hallway's two long walls, floor and ceiling from one end to the other, running east with its walls at south and north, a rail along each wall
: east-hall-shell ( west east south north height -- )
	| west east south north height |
	0.45 pen!
	[ [ west 0 south ] [ east 0 south ] [ east height south ] ] path
	[ [ west 0 north ] [ east 0 north ] [ east height north ] ] path
	west height south east height south edge
	west height north east height north edge
	east 0 south east 0 north edge
	east height south east height north edge
	0.2 pen!
	west 0.95 south east 0.95 south edge
	west 0.95 north east 0.95 north edge ;

\ the west part of the south hallway, seen from the archway at the foot of the stairs: Mrs. Rourke's door in the south wall, the hall going on east
: shall-1-picture ( -- )
	-0.5 1.65 0.7 1.78 -0.06 260 new-picture
	[ 3.5 2.3 1.1 ] lamp!
	[ [ [ 3.3 0 0.2 ] PI 2 / PI + 0.3 - ] [ [ 4.7 0 -0.4 ] PI 2 / PI + ] [ [ 2.4 0 0.7 ] PI 2 / PI + 0.4 + ] ] spots!
	0.1 pen!
	-0.8 7 -1.2 1.2 0.25 false plank-floor
	-0.8 7 -1.2 1.2 3 east-hall-shell
	0.45 pen!
	-0.8 0 -1.2 -0.8 3 -1.2 edge
	0.45 pen!
	7 -0.45 7 0.45 2.1 :rourke-bath-door :open flag? -1 0 wall-panel-door
	5.4 -1.2 6.1 -1.2 1.9 :south-closet-door :open flag? 0 -1 wall-panel-door
	0.55 pen!
	1.4 -1.2 2.3 -1.2 2.2 :rourke-door :open flag? 0 -1 wall-panel-door
	:rourke-door :open flag? if
		0.08 pen!
		1.5 0 -1.2 1.4 0 -3 edge
		2.2 0 -1.2 2.4 0 -3 edge
	then
	3.5 2.2 1.2 0 -1 hallway-sconce ;

\ the east end of the south hallway, seen coming from the west: the bathroom door at the end, the small closet door in the south wall
: shall-2-picture ( -- )
	-0.4 1.65 0.3 PI 2 / 0.08 + -0.06 260 new-picture
	[ 2 2.7 0 ] lamp!
	[ [ [ 2.9 0 0.5 ] PI 2 / PI + 0.2 - ] [ [ 2.5 0 -0.5 ] PI 2 / PI + 0.4 + ] ] spots!
	0.1 pen!
	-0.5 3.6 -1.2 1.2 0.25 false plank-floor
	-0.5 3.6 -1.2 1.2 3 east-hall-shell
	0.6 pen!
	3.6 -0.45 3.6 0.45 2.1 :rourke-bath-door :open flag? -1 0 wall-panel-door
	:rourke-bath-door :open flag? if
		0.1 pen!
		3.6 0 -0.4 5.2 0 -0.4 edge
		3.6 0 0.4 5.2 0 0.4 edge
		[ 5 1 0 ] 0.6 0.06 glow
	then
	0.55 pen!
	2.7 -1.2 2.0 -1.2 1.8 :south-closet-door :open flag? 0 1 wall-panel-door
	2 2.75 0 3 pendant-lamp ;

\ === the South Closet ===

\ a bare light bulb hanging on its cord, with a pull chain
: closet-light ( x y z ceiling -- )
	| x y z ceiling |
	[ x y z ] 0.9 0.4 glow
	0.4 pen!
	x ceiling z x y 0.05 + z edge
	0.9 pen!
	x y z 0.035 8 ring outline
	x y 0.05 + z 0.02 6 ring outline
	0.3 pen!
	x 0.02 + y z x 0.02 + y 0.35 - z edge ;

\ the little storage closet, seen from its door: shelves of boxes and cans, a broom and a bucket, under a bare bulb
: south-closet-picture ( -- )
	0 1.65 1.2 PI -0.16 250 new-picture
	[ 0 2.2 -1.1 ] lamp!
	[ [ [ 0.1 0 -1.2 ] PI 0.1 + ] ] spots!
	0.1 pen!
	-1 1 -2.2 0 0.2 true plank-floor
	0.45 pen!
	-1 1 -2.2 0 2.6 room-shell
	[ -1 0.62 ] ( wall-x |
		0 4 1 do shelf
			shelf 0.5 * 0.3 + to board
			0.4 pen!
			wall-x board -2.15 wall-x 0.38 + board 0.03 + -1.0 solid-box
			0 5 1 do slot
				wall-x 1234 * shelf 77 * + slot 13 * + hash-fraction to chance
				chance 0.3 > if
					slot 0.22 * -2.1 + to box-south
					chance 0.14 * 0.1 + to box-height
					0.3 chance 0.35 * + pen!
					wall-x 0.06 + board 0.03 + box-south wall-x 0.3 + board 0.03 + box-height + box-south 0.18 + solid-box
				then
			loop
		loop
	) each
	0.45 pen!
	[ [ -0.45 0 -2.1 ] [ -0.2 1.5 -2.15 ] ] path
	[ [ -0.45 0 -2.1 ] [ -0.58 -0.02 -1.95 ] ] path
	[ [ -0.45 0 -2.1 ] [ -0.33 -0.02 -1.97 ] ] path
	0.5 pen!
	0.2 0.3 -1.7 0.14 10 ring outline
	0.2 0 -1.7 0.11 10 ring outline
	0 10 2 do k
		k 10 / TAU * to angle
		0.2 angle cos 0.11 * + 0 -1.7 angle sin 0.11 * +
		0.2 angle cos 0.14 * + 0.3 -1.7 angle sin 0.14 * + edge
	loop
	0 1.95 -1.1 2.6 closet-light ;

\ === Mrs. Rourke's rooms ===

\ a plain wooden chair: seat, four legs and a back, placed at a spot facing a heading
: rourke-chair ( spot heading -- )
	| spot heading |
	[ [ -0.2 0 -0.2 ] [ 0.2 0 -0.2 ] [ 0.2 0 0.2 ] [ -0.2 0 0.2 ] ]
	( corner | corner spread to cz drop to cx [ [ cx 0 cz ] [ cx 0.45 cz ] ] spot heading turned-path ) each
	[ -0.22 0.43 -0.22 ] [ 0.22 0.48 0.22 ] spot heading turned-box
	[ -0.21 0.48 -0.22 ] [ 0.21 0.95 -0.19 ] spot heading turned-box ;

\ Mrs. Rourke's bedroom, seen from its door: the single bed under the closed south window, bare end tables either side, the hardwood floor
: rourke-room-picture ( -- )
	0.4 1.65 1.1 PI 0.06 + -0.12 255 new-picture
	[ 0 1.6 -3.4 ] lamp!
	[ [ [ -1.15 0 -1.9 ] 0.25 ] [ [ 1.25 0 -1.8 ] -0.3 ] [ [ 0.1 0 -0.8 ] 0.1 ] ] spots!
	[ 0 1.55 -3.2 ] 1.4 0.2 glow
	0.12 pen!
	-1.8 1.8 -3.2 0 0.18 true plank-floor
	-0.6 0 1.0 2.1 -3.2 south-pane-light
	0 0.6 1.0 2.1 -3.2 south-pane-light
	0.45 pen!
	-1.8 1.8 -3.2 0 2.9 room-shell
	0.8 pen!
	[ [ -0.6 1.0 -3.2 ] [ 0.6 1.0 -3.2 ] [ 0.6 2.1 -3.2 ] [ -0.6 2.1 -3.2 ] ] outline
	0 1.0 -3.2 0 2.1 -3.2 edge
	-0.6 1.55 -3.2 0.6 1.55 -3.2 edge
	0.35 pen!
	[ [ -0.7 0.95 -3.19 ] [ 0.7 0.95 -3.19 ] ] path
	[ -1.8 0 -2.2 ] PI 2 / rourke-chair
	0.5 pen!
	-1.05 0 -3.2 -0.62 0.55 -2.8 solid-box
	0.62 0 -3.2 1.05 0.55 -2.8 solid-box
	0.45 pen!
	-0.55 0 -3.2 0.55 0.95 -3.12 solid-box
	0.55 pen!
	-0.5 0.25 -3.12 0.5 0.45 -1.2 solid-box
	0.35 pen!
	[ [ -0.5 0.46 -2.9 ] [ 0.5 0.46 -2.9 ] ] path
	[ [ -0.47 0.46 -3.08 ] [ 0.47 0.46 -3.08 ] [ 0.47 0.52 -2.75 ] [ -0.47 0.52 -2.75 ] ] outline
	[ [ -0.5 0.45 -2.5 ] [ -0.5 0.05 -2.45 ] ] path
	[ [ 0.5 0.45 -2.5 ] [ 0.5 0.05 -2.45 ] ] path
	[ [ -0.5 0.05 -2.45 ] [ -0.5 0.05 -1.2 ] ] path
	[ [ 0.5 0.05 -2.45 ] [ 0.5 0.05 -1.2 ] ] path ;

\ a toilet: its tank against the wall, the bowl before it, the seat on the bowl
: water-closet ( spot heading -- )
	| spot heading |
	[ -0.2 0.4 -0.02 ] [ 0.2 0.8 0.17 ] spot heading turned-box
	[ -0.1 0 0.17 ] [ 0.1 0.36 0.4 ] spot heading turned-box
	[ [ 0 0.41 0.17 ] [ 0.16 0.41 0.2 ] [ 0.2 0.41 0.32 ] [ 0.14 0.41 0.44 ] [ 0 0.41 0.47 ]
	  [ -0.14 0.41 0.44 ] [ -0.2 0.41 0.32 ] [ -0.16 0.41 0.2 ] ] ( point | point spot heading placed ) map to seat
	seat 0 fill
	pen to fixture-light
	fixture-light 1.3 * pen!
	seat outline
	fixture-light pen! ;

\ a washbasin on its pedestal, its tap behind the bowl
: washbasin ( spot heading -- )
	| spot heading |
	[ -0.08 0 0.05 ] [ 0.08 0.72 0.2 ] spot heading turned-box
	[ -0.28 0.72 0 ] [ 0.28 0.86 0.42 ] spot heading turned-box
	pen to fixture-light
	fixture-light 0.8 * pen!
	[ [ -0.22 0.86 0.08 ] [ 0.22 0.86 0.08 ] [ 0.22 0.86 0.36 ] [ -0.22 0.86 0.36 ] ] spot heading turned-path
	fixture-light 1.3 * pen!
	[ [ 0 0.86 0.04 ] [ 0 0.95 0.04 ] [ 0 0.95 0.12 ] ] spot heading turned-path
	fixture-light pen! ;

\ a shower stall in a corner: its tray, the corner post and the curtain hanging in folds from its rail
: shower-stall ( x0 z0 x1 z1 -- )
	| x0 z0 x1 z1 |
	x0 0 z0 x1 0.12 z1 solid-box
	[ [ x0 2.1 z1 ] [ x1 2.1 z1 ] [ x1 2.1 z0 ] ] path
	pen to stall-light
	stall-light 0.6 * pen!
	0 9 1 do k
		k 8 / to along
		x0 x1 x0 - along * + to x
		x 0.14 z1 x k 2 mod 0.04 * + 2.05 z1 0.03 - edge
	loop
	stall-light pen! ;

\ Mrs. Rourke's bathroom, seen from its door: the toilet and the washbasin, the shower in the corner, two shelves of bottles on the wall
: rourke-bath-picture ( -- )
	-1.3 1.65 0.1 PI 2 / 0.08 + -0.16 245 new-picture
	[ 1.3 2.5 0 ] lamp!
	[ [ [ 1.3 0 0.15 ] PI 2 / PI + 0.2 + ] [ [ 0.8 0 -0.6 ] PI 2 / PI + 0.4 - ] ] spots!
	0.12 pen!
	[ 0 0 -1.2 ] [ 2.6 0 -1.2 ] [ 2.6 0 1.2 ] [ 0 0 1.2 ] 8 8 grid
	0.45 pen!
	0 2.6 -1.2 1.2 2.7 room-shell
	0.5 pen!
	1.7 -1.2 2.6 -0.3 shower-stall
	0.6 pen!
	[ 2.6 0 0.55 ] PI -2 / water-closet
	[ 1.3 0 1.2 ] PI washbasin
	0.5 pen!
	[ 0.5 1.25 ] ( height |
		0.3 height 1.1 1.3 height 0.03 + 1.2 solid-box
		0 5 1 do k
			k 7 * height 100 * + hash-fraction to chance
			0.35 k 0.19 * + to bottle-x
			0.4 chance 0.4 * + pen!
			bottle-x height 0.03 + 1.15 0.025 detail-scale * 8 ring to bottle-base
			bottle-x height 0.03 + chance 0.1 * + 0.12 + 1.15 0.025 detail-scale * 8 ring to bottle-top
			bottle-base outline
			bottle-top outline
			bottle-base 0 @i bottle-top 0 @i segment
			bottle-base 4 @i bottle-top 4 @i segment
		loop
	) each
	1.3 2.4 0 2.7 closet-light ;

\ === the Living Room ===

\ the heading from a spot toward a point on the floor
: heading-toward ( x z target-x target-z -- heading )
	| x z target-x target-z |
	target-x x - target-z z - atan2 ;

\ a couch or an armchair, length wide, its seat facing forward: the seat, its back behind and an arm at each end
: sofa-piece ( spot heading length -- )
	| spot heading length |
	length 2 / to half
	[ half negate 0 -0.45 ] [ half 0.9 -0.25 ] spot heading turned-box
	[ half negate 0 -0.25 ] [ half 0.45 0.45 ] spot heading turned-box
	[ half negate 0 -0.45 ] [ half negate 0.15 + 0.62 0.45 ] spot heading turned-box
	[ half 0.15 - 0 -0.45 ] [ half 0.62 0.45 ] spot heading turned-box
	pen to seat-light
	seat-light 0.5 * pen!
	[ [ 0 0.45 -0.25 ] [ 0 0.45 0.45 ] ] spot heading turned-path
	seat-light pen! ;

\ a low table on four legs
: coffee-table ( x z width depth -- )
	| x z width depth |
	x width 2 / - to west
	x width 2 / + to east
	z depth 2 / - to south
	z depth 2 / + to north
	[ [ west 0.06 + south 0.06 + ] [ east 0.06 - south 0.06 + ] [ east 0.06 - north 0.06 - ] [ west 0.06 + north 0.06 - ] ]
	( corner | corner spread to leg-z to leg-x leg-x 0 leg-z leg-x 0 0.38 + leg-z edge ) each
	west 0.38 south east 0.44 north solid-box ;

\ a cabinet against the north wall, its doors facing south: the box, the join between its doors and their handles
: walnut-cabinet ( west east south north height -- )
	| west east south north height |
	west 0 south east height north solid-box
	west east + 2 / to middle
	pen to cabinet-light
	cabinet-light 0.6 * pen!
	middle 0.08 south middle height 0.08 - south edge
	cabinet-light 1.3 * pen!
	middle 0.06 - height 0.55 * south middle 0.06 - height 0.45 * south edge
	middle 0.06 + height 0.55 * south middle 0.06 + height 0.45 * south edge
	cabinet-light pen! ;

\ an oval of points on a wall around a centre, rx along the wall and ry up it
: wall-oval ( centre along rx ry count -- points )
	| centre along rx ry count |
	[ 0 count 1 do k
		k count / TAU * to angle
		centre along angle cos rx * angle sin ry * wall-at
	loop ] ;

\ a framed portrait on a wall: the frame, the oval within, and the sitter's head and shoulders in shadow
: portrait-frame ( corner along width height -- )
	| corner along width height |
	corner along 0 0 wall-at corner along width 0 wall-at
	corner along width height wall-at corner along 0 height wall-at 4 array to frame
	frame 0 fill
	pen to frame-light
	frame outline
	corner along width 2 / height 2 / wall-at to middle
	frame-light 0.5 * pen!
	middle along width 0.36 * height 0.4 * 14 wall-oval outline
	middle along 0 height 0.08 * wall-at along width 0.1 * height 0.14 * 10 wall-oval to face
	face 0.06 fill
	frame-light 0.7 * pen!
	face outline
	[ middle along width -0.22 * height -0.3 * wall-at middle along width -0.12 * height -0.12 * wall-at
	  middle along width 0.12 * height -0.12 * wall-at middle along width 0.22 * height -0.3 * wall-at ] path
	frame-light pen! ;

\ a chimney breast of fieldstone standing out from the west wall: the stones in rough courses, the dark firebox and the hearth before it
: fieldstone-chimney ( wall-x south north height -- )
	| wall-x south north height |
	wall-x 0.5 + to face-x
	wall-x 0 south face-x height north solid-box
	pen to stone-light
	0 to course-bottom
	0 to course
	begin course-bottom height < while
		course 31 * hash-fraction 0.08 * 0.2 + to course-height
		course 2 mod 0.18 * south + to seam
		stone-light 0.45 * pen!
		face-x 0.02 + course-bottom south face-x 0.02 + course-bottom north edge
		begin seam north < while
			seam course 7 * + 13 * hash-fraction 0.22 * 0.28 + seam + to next-seam
			next-seam north min2 to next-seam
			face-x 0.02 + course-bottom seam face-x 0.02 + course-bottom course-height + seam edge
			next-seam to seam
		repeat
		course-bottom course-height + to course-bottom
		++ course
	repeat
	south north + 2 / to middle
	[ [ face-x 0.01 + 0 middle 0.55 - ] [ face-x 0.01 + 0 middle 0.55 + ] [ face-x 0.01 + 0.85 middle 0.55 + ] [ face-x 0.01 + 0.85 middle 0.55 - ] ] to firebox
	firebox 0 fill
	stone-light 1.2 * pen!
	firebox outline
	stone-light pen!
	face-x 0 middle 0.8 - face-x 0.6 + 0.08 middle 0.8 + solid-box ;

\ a stack of split logs against the west wall, their cut ends toward the room
: log-pile ( wall-x south -- )
	| wall-x south |
	[ 0 0 1 ] to across
	[ 0 1 0 ] to upward
	[ [ 0 0 ] [ 1 0 ] [ 2 0 ] [ 0.5 1 ] [ 1.5 1 ] [ 1 2 ] ] ( place |
		place spread to row to column
		[ wall-x 0.55 + row 0.17 * 0.09 + south column 0.19 * + 0.09 + ] to log-centre
		log-centre across upward 0.085 10 circle-points to log-end
		log-end 0 fill
		log-end outline
		log-centre across upward 0.04 8 circle-points outline
	) each ;

\ a telephone on a table top: its base and the handset in its cradle
: telephone-set ( x y z heading -- )
	| x y z heading |
	[ x y z ] to spot
	( point | point ( coordinate | coordinate detail-scale * ) map ) to enlarged
	[ -0.07 0 -0.06 ] enlarged execute [ 0.07 0.06 0.06 ] enlarged execute spot heading turned-box
	pen to phone-light
	phone-light 1.3 * pen!
	[ [ -0.1 0.09 0 ] [ -0.07 0.1 0 ] [ 0.07 0.1 0 ] [ 0.1 0.09 0 ] ] enlarged map spot heading turned-path
	[ [ -0.1 0.09 0 ] [ -0.1 0.07 0 ] ] enlarged map spot heading turned-path
	[ [ 0.1 0.09 0 ] [ 0.1 0.07 0 ] ] enlarged map spot heading turned-path
	phone-light pen! ;

\ the living room, seen from the double doorway to the east: the bay window to the south with the family portraits about it, the fieldstone fireplace and wood pile to the west, groups of couches and chairs, the cabinets, and the telephone on its table
: living-room-picture ( -- )
	5.3 1.65 2.9 -2.3 -0.09 245 new-picture
